<title>INDIA: Indian soybean down, soyoil up, soymeal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean down, soyoil up, soymeal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were down by 200-300 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Friday, dealers said. Arrivals were around 1,200 tonnes. Business volume was dull and undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand in local market. trading activity was thin and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were bearish. Soymeal yellow was $310-312 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports. Rapeseed extraction was $111-113 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export and was 3,950-4,000 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was very dull and the undertone was easy. Selling and demand both were at lowest level for export trading.</p>
